* Provenance: written for circsim from manufacturer datasheet parameters, MIT.
* In-house LED .model cards. An LED is a diode whose forward drop is set by its
* die material; we reproduce the datasheet typical Vf at the rated test current
* by raising the emission coefficient n and the bandgap eg (eg shifts the
* temperature behavior toward the wider-gap III-V material; n widens the
* exponential so the knee lands at the right voltage). No vendor model text is
* copied — only the datasheet Vf/If operating points inform the fit.
*
* Target forward drops (typical @ ~20 mA):
*   red    ~1.8-2.0 V   (AlGaInP / GaAsP)
*   green  ~2.1-2.2 V   (InGaN, traditional green ~2.2 V)
*   blue   ~3.0-3.2 V   (InGaN)
*   white  ~3.0-3.4 V   (blue InGaN die + phosphor)
*
* Cj is set ~15-50 pF (small indicator LED). Reverse Vbr ~5 V typical.

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- RED
.model LED_RED D(is=1e-19 rs=2.0 n=1.7 cjo=30p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5 ibv=100u eg=1.9 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- GREEN
.model LED_GREEN D(is=1e-20 rs=3.0 n=1.8 cjo=30p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5 ibv=100u eg=2.1 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- BLUE
.model LED_BLUE D(is=1e-26 rs=6.0 n=1.9 cjo=20p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5 ibv=100u eg=2.9 xti=3)

* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- WHITE
.model LED_WHITE D(is=1e-26 rs=7.0 n=1.9 cjo=20p vj=0.75 m=0.333
+ bv=5 ibv=100u eg=3.0 xti=3)
